    "independent": false,
    "summary": "Built the internal document library for the NocoBase 3 app: registered the library.documents composite business operation with own/published/nonConfidential/readable record-access scopes and a confidentiality Restriction Rule; added a documents migration with a string primary key plus a libraryProvisioning marker; added the /api/documents REST routes with describeRoute/apiValidator authorization and repository policy binding; added the /documents list page, create dialog, detail drawer and stacked edit dialog with navigation and translations; and provisioned the 资料员甲/阅读者乙 accounts, the library-maintainer/library-reader permission sets and the P/D/C sample documents exactly once at boot. All five previously failing browser criteria now hold, verified end to end against a fresh migrated database. Repair-3 reconciled pnpm-lock.yaml with package.json so the frozen-lockfile check passes again.",
    "blockers": [],
    "improvements": [
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37700953909/attempt/1/I1",
        "category": "template",
        "title": "Make the string-id requirement for per-record sharing explicit",
        "detail": "The authorization layer's record selection schema only accepts string ids, so any Collection that should support Sharing Rules must use a string primary key. An integer primary key builds, boots and serves normally, then fails a share with a 400 INVALID_FILTER that names only the field type.",
        "suggestedChange": "Document this at the Sharing Rules reference and at the Collection builder, or coerce/validate selection ids against the target field type when a rule is created.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37700953909/attempt/1/I2",
        "category": "tooling",
        "title": "Warn when a granted composite action has no database policy branch",
        "detail": "A composite authorization decision can be `conditional` with no policy for the configured collection, and the route then has to invent a per-action denial. A boot-time validation could report a composite action whose grants never produce a database condition.",
        "suggestedChange": "Extend the authorization startup checks to report composite actions with no reachable database policy.",
        "mechanizable": true
      },
      {
        "id": "notes/run/37700953909/attempt/1/I3",
        "category": "tooling",
        "title": "Refresh the lockfile after correcting shadcn's package.json edits",
        "detail": "The shadcn add workflow writes pnpm-lock.yaml itself, pinning @nocobase/i18n to an exact version and adding client-only packages under importer dependencies. The documented correction is to restore the ^ range and move the package to devDependencies in package.json, but the lockfile is then stale and every later frozen-lockfile install fails with ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE.",
        "suggestedChange": "State in the shadcn reference that after editing package.json the lockfile must be regenerated with `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile`, or have the CLI leave the lockfile to the next install.",
        "mechanizable": true
      }
    ],
    "note": "实现者自述，未经独立核验；不是框架评审结论。"
  },
